content.text:
Add small styles for mat-cycle spans and rotate. Also result screen hidden via `.overlay.hidden` works. Now main.js.

Need maybe set canvas context imageSmoothing default true. fine.

Main:
```js
import { Game } ...
const canvas...
const audio = new AudioEngine();
const game = new Game(canvas, audio);
const renderer = new Renderer(game);
const ui = new UI(game, audio);
game.setUI? ui constructor does.
window resize.
let last=performance.now();
function frame(now){...}
```
Important Game constructor calls `this.resize(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight)` before UI created; controls layout exists; good.
- UI constructor accesses `game.makePiece` etc via sync? syncAll->syncWeapon calls g.buildCost; okay. sync calls buildTeamChips; game default demo has worms and seed. good.
- `UI` imports from game.js causing circular? ui imports game.js constants; game doesn't import ui. main imports both. fine.

Pointer:
```
let activePointer=null;
canvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', e=>{
 if(e.pointerType==='mouse' && e.button!==0) return;
 e.preventDefault();
 if(activePointer!==null) return;
 activePointer=e.pointerId;
 canvas.setPointerCapture?.(e.pointerId);
 game.pointerDown(e.clientX,e.clientY);
});
canvas.addEventListener('pointermove', e=>{
 if(activePointer !== null && e.pointerId !== activePointer) return;
 game.pointerMove(e.clientX,e.clientY, activePointer!==null);
});
canvas.addEventListener('pointerup', e=>{ if(activePointer!==e.pointerId)return; activePointer=null; game.pointerUp();});
...
```
- For hover build ghost: pointermove without down calls game.pointerMove(...,false). But game.pointerMove requires state aim and player; good.
- On mobile, if pointer down starts on canvas and moves over UI footer, pointer capture means it still goes to canvas; game.inField guard ignores below field, but aim stops updating; release triggers fire (fireActive) if aiming. If user drags into footer accidentally, still fires. okay.
- Prevent context menu.
- Wheel? no.
- Keyboard:
  - Use `e.key.toLowerCase()`. Don't handle when help open except Escape.
  - If input focused? no inputs.
  - On keydown repeat: movement fine; jump should only on !repeat; mode/select only !repeat.
  - `event.code` for Space.
  - `Escape` if result? no; if help -> close.
  - `h` open help.
  - `Enter` end turn.
  - When not playing (start screen), ignore gameplay keys.
- Window blur: clear keys.
- Resize: `requestAnimationFrame(() => { game.resize(...); ui.measure(); })`; ResizeObserver controls.
- `document.fonts.ready.then(() => ui.measure())`.
- Start screen visible, UI sync maybe.
- Debug:
```
window.__buildBlast = { game, renderer, ui, audio, start: ()=>ui.startMatch(), build: (...), shot: ... , get state(){...} }
```
- Maybe expose a test function to simulate AI turns? Could call game.startMatch, game.fireActive, etc. For verification, we can use page.evaluate.
- Error logging to console.

Game loop:
```
if (!document.hidden || true) { game.update(dt); renderer.render(); }
requestAnimationFrame
```
- If game.paused, game.update returns before time; renderer still renders. Good.

Add `visibilitychange` to reset last time and clear keys.

Potential important bug: UI constructor `syncAll` calls `syncWeapon` which calls `g.buildCost` (exists). `this.el.matCount` exists. `buildTeamChips` uses `g.seed`; exists. fine.

Potential important bug: Game `startMatch` calls `this.reset(finalSeed,false)` and then `startTurn`; but reset's `this.fx` new means UI? fine. UI setPlaying/hideStart after startTurn; startTurn calls ui.syncAll and banner. UI still hidden but okay.
- `startTurn` sets state, calls `this.ui?.banner`; banner shows behind start? start screen hides in same tick after startTurn, then banner visible. Good.
- `startMatch` calls `ui.setPlaying(true)` then `ui.hideStart()`; setPlaying app.playing, start screen still visible until hide. fine.

Potential bug: Game reset sets `this.time` not reset; time continues from load, builder builtAt uses time; fine.
- FX new but time continues; fine.

Potential bug: Game reset with demo true sets state demo but `this.ui` maybe not set yet; no calls.
- `this.camX` not reset; startMatch after demo camera stays; fine.

Potential bug: `this.windDisplay` set in reset, startTurn; okay.

Need use `rand` import in game; yes.

Let's write main.

