content.text:
Now edit mobile media block. Replace the relevant sections. Current lines 746-844. Let me make targeted edits:

1. `.team-card` currently height 52 etc. Keep.
2. Replace `.team-name { display: none; }` with short name display.
3. Replace `.team-topline` justification (currently flex-end) with space-between, and team-b same.
4. Replace controls/profile/action/hotbar rules.

Let's craft.

For mobile:
```
.team-card { height: 52px; padding: 6px 8px; gap: 5px; }
.team-emblem { width: 22px; height: 22px; }
.team-name { display: block; font-size: 7.5px; letter-spacing: .04em; }
.tn-full { display: none; }
.tn-short { display: inline; }
.team-topline { justify-content: space-between; gap: 4px; }
.team-b .team-topline { justify-content: space-between; }
.team-hp { font-size: 13px; }
```
At 390 card 129: content 129-16-5-22=86; HP 25 + gap 4 → name 57; short fits. Good.
At 320 card 94: content 94-16-5-22=51; HP 25 + gap4 → name 22; "SUNSET" at 7.5px ~25 → slight clip with ellipsis. Could reduce emblem to 20 and padding 6 → content 94-12-5-20=57, name 28, fits. Let's use padding 5px 7px, emblem 22, gap 5 → content 94-14-5-22=53, name 24. "SUNSET" ~24 at 7.5px maybe. Use font 7px letter-spacing .02em. Fine. At 390 name 57 plenty.

Worm chips: at 320 chip width (53-4)/2=24.5; "BISCUIT" at 6px ~21 fits barely; "PEBBLE" ~20. Right. At 390 chip width (86-4)/2=41, fine.

Now controls:
```
.controls {
  --controls-h: 142px;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr) auto;
  grid-template-rows: auto auto;
  gap: 6px;
  ...
}
.active-profile {
  position: static;
  grid-row: 1; grid-column: 1;
  width: auto;
  padding: 5px 7px; gap: 6px;
  ...
}
.hotbar-wrap { grid-row:2; grid-column:1/-1; ... }
.action-stack {
  grid-row:1; grid-column:2;
  max-width:none;
  flex-direction:row;
  align-items:center;
  gap:6px;
  padding-left:0;
  justify-self:end;
}
.mode-btn { flex: 1; min-width: 0; height:34px; ... }
.end-btn { flex:0 0 78px; height:34px; ...}
```
Compute row: profile width available = 370 - 6 - (mode content + end 78). Action stack width auto = mode natural width + gap + end. Mode natural content: icon16 + gap8 + text ~34 + padding 18 = 76. So action = 76+6+78=160. Profile gets 204. Great. At 320: controls content 300; action 160; profile 134. Good. End right = 390-10=380. 

Mode button `flex:1` within action stack: width auto = content 76. Fine.

Hotbar row spans full width, centered. Good.

`--controls-h` actual: row1 max(profile height ~44, 34)=44 + gap 6 + hotbar 55 + padding top10+bottom8=123. So 123. touch-move bottom calc(var(--controls-h)+56) = 179. Buttons bottom at 844-179=665, top 617. Previously buttons at 625-675. Slight raise 8px. Fine. Could set +48 to keep 625. With controls-h 123, +48=171, bottom 673, top 625. Let's use +48 for mobile. Toast bottom calc(controls-h + 116) = 239, fine.

Profile bottom no longer absolute; remove `bottom`.

Also `.profile-label { display:none }` already.

Landscape: the max-height 500 block must reset grid-column for the three items:
```
.active-profile { position: static; width:auto; grid-column:auto; ... max-width: 250px; justify-self:start; }
.action-stack { grid-row:auto; grid-column:auto; ...}
.hotbar-wrap { grid-row:auto; grid-column:auto; ...}
```
And maybe max-width profile. Also in landscape, team names: the max-width 780 doesn't apply (844), but `(pointer: coarse)` applies so mobile HUD rules apply including `.tn-full{display:none}` etc. Then landscape overrides `.team-name { display:block; font-size:8px; letter-spacing:.07em; }` but tn-full remains hidden and tn-short visible from mobile. We want full names in landscape since there's width. Add in landscape:
```
.tn-full { display:inline; }
.tn-short { display:none; }
```
Also `.team-emblem` 24. Fine.

Landscape `.team-name` 8px, full names fit: card width (844-20-96-10)/2=359; plenty.

Also landscape `.controls` height 64; `--controls-h: 86px` on .controls but ui.measure sets root 64. Not an issue, but remove 86 to avoid confusion? It affects touch-move bottom: `.touch-move { bottom: calc(var(--controls-h) + 8px) }` uses root var 64 → 72. Fine. The `.controls` local var only affects descendants? `.toast` uses root var. Leave.

Let's apply edits.

